# rogue3#46. TemplateDrift pins a sha256 over all 190 files under `.agents/skills/**` and
# `.claude/skills/**` and requires the two trees to stay byte-identical. Git's default
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows rewrites every text file on checkout, which changes those
# bytes and makes the gate red on a correct clone — the failure mode `build.fsx` is written
# throughout to avoid.
#
# Pinning EOL here is what makes "190 of 190" a property of the repository rather than of the
# platform that happened to clone it. Filed as #62 item 5 and brought forward into #46 on a
# reviewer's argument: this item is what raises the affected surface from 64 files to 190, so
# it is the item that should carry the one-line fix.
#
# `text eol=lf` normalises to LF in the index and checks out LF everywhere. The kit is all
# text (`.md`, `.yaml`, `.json`, `.fs`, `.fsx`, `.py`), so this is safe and keeps diffs textual;
# `-text` would also stabilise the bytes but would make every kit file diff as binary.
.agents/skills/** text eol=lf
.claude/skills/** text eol=lf

# The two files the gate reads as its oracles, for the same reason.
scripts/kit-pins.json text eol=lf
